WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.700
Good morning, John.

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.580
This video comes to you in 54 parts,

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:04.820
each of which will explain how to register to vote,

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:05.700
how to get a sample ballot,

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:07.660
and how to vote in each of the 50 states,

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:09.580
as well as in a few other cases,

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:12.120
because we are the United States of America,

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:15.280
and each state establishes its own laws and procedures,

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:17.320
so the process of voting is different

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:18.120
everywhere.

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:20.440
It's just part of what makes America beautiful,

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:21.920
and a little bit annoying.

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:23.520
But, yes, we did put together

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:25.980
over 30,000 words of scripts for this project

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:26.820
and, yes,

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:28.040
it was a bit of a pain.

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:28.540
But, it's worth it,

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:32.460
because I feel that voting is one of the most important parts of being an American.

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:34.140
There are a lot of different ways to vote

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:35.480
not just practically,

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:36.480
depending on where you live,

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:37.780
but philosophically,

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:40.240
you can vote for the world you most want to see,

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:43.840
or you can vote for the world you think will most likely bring change,

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:47.460
or you can vote for just one thing, or based on just one thing,

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:49.400
how you want to vote is up to you.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:50.600
As is whether you vote.

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:55.040
But, I want to make sure that you understand that not voting isn't some revolutionary political act,

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:58.020
if you're not voting, no-one is hearing your voice,

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:00.260
so they have no reason to represent you.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:01.320
Depending on where you live,

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:02.380
registering and voting

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:04.080
are varying degrees of difficult,

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:04.980
but, in these videos,

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:06.100
I'm making it clear.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.600
If you don't think that voting matters because no one voter decides an election,

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:10.400
two things:

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:12.060
One, if everybody thought that way,

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:12.920
nobody would vote,

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:16.060
except for one guy who was just drunk and stumbled into the polling place

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:18.560
and he would decide how the entire country got run.

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:19.680
So, it does matter.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:22.520
If everyone who watches this video goes out and votes,

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:23.320
we will,

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:24.180
we, us,

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:25.760
will be an important voting bloc.

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:28.480
Second, the majority of government in America is local,

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:32.500
and local elections do, in fact, frequently get decided by one person.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:34.780
This is how change happens,

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:38.420
especially as national government has become less effective in recent years.

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:40.240
This is how laws get made,

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:42.660
and how rights get granted or taken away.

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:44.500
If you don't feel informed on every issue,

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:48.140
it's easy to get a sample ballot, which I'll explain in your state's video,

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:49.420
and to do some research.

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:53.660
It just takes an hour, or half-hour, of research, to help make America a better place.

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:54.540
It's not hard.

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:57.580
It might be a little complicated, but we're going to solve that problem right now.

00:01:57.580 --> 00:02:00.380
Please send this video, or the corresponding state video,

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:02.460
to everyone you know who might not vote

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:03.920
because it's too complicated,

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:05.160
or they're not sure how.

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:07.280
We do not change this country as individuals,

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:09.200
we change it as an electorate.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:11.720
It might not be fast, it might not be perfect,

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:13.920
but democracy does not work

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:15.520
if we do not participate.

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:17.480
You can now click on your state's name

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:19.960
to watch the video on how to make sure you're registered,

00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:22.060
to register, to get your sample ballot,

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:22.780
and vote.

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:24.420
John, I'll see you on Tuesday.

